# Airrow runs fully in local mode with no env vars required (ADR-0005).
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill only the integrations you want to activate.

# ── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloud: from Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API.
# Local dev (`supabase start`): the CLI prints these; the local defaults are stable.
#   URL         → http://127.0.0.1:54321
#   anon key    → the "anon key" line printed by `supabase start` / `supabase status`
#   service key → the "service_role key" line (server-only — never expose to the client)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Direct Postgres connection (used by the RLS integration test against local Supabase).
# Cloud: Supabase → Project Settings → Database → Connection string (URI).
# Local default:
#   postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
SUPABASE_DB_URL=

# ── Claude authoring provider (replaces local deterministic authoring) ───────
# Without a key, generation is fully deterministic and still delivers a ZIP — the key turns on the
# LLM-authored prose (spec 65), it is not required to run the app.
# From console.anthropic.com → API keys. This is Developer Platform billing, separate from any
# Claude subscription, and the org needs credits before the first call succeeds.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Overrides the authoring model. Defaults to claude-haiku-4-5; set claude-opus-5 to compare quality.
# AIRROW_AUTHORING_MODEL=

# ── Landing chat (spec 141) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A key of its own, from a separate console.anthropic.com workspace with its own spend limit. The
# chat is a public, unauthenticated surface; ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is deliberately never used as a
# fallback, so a wave of abuse against the chat cannot reach generation's budget.
# AIRROW_CHAT_API_KEY=
# Salt for the visitor hash the daily limit is counted against. Any long random string; keep it
# secret and stable, since changing it resets every visitor's allowance.
# AIRROW_CHAT_IP_SALT=
# Overrides the chat model. Defaults to claude-haiku-4-5.
# AIRROW_CHAT_MODEL=
#
# Missing either of the first two, or a database that has not run the chat migration, turns the panel
# off rather than loose: it shows its handwritten answers instead of calling anything.

# ── GitHub App delivery (enables push-to-GitHub) ────────────────────────────
# GITHUB_APP_ID=
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
# GITHUB_APP_SLUG=

# ── Auth email sending via Resend (spec 113) ────────────────────────────────
# The hosted project sends through Resend so the verification email comes from Airrow instead of from
# Supabase — configured in the Supabase dashboard, not here (INFRASTRUCTURE_SETUP.md §6).
# You only need this key to test real delivery from your own machine, and doing so means uncommenting
# `[auth.email.smtp]` in supabase/config.toml, which stops mail going to the local inbox and starts
# mailing real addresses. By default local development sends nothing outward.
#
# The same key is what the app itself sends support tickets and reviews with (spec 144) — over
# Resend's HTTP API rather than SMTP, from `lib/email.ts`. Without it those still save; only the
# notification to us is skipped, which is the right default on a developer machine.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
#
# Where founder mail is delivered, and who it comes from. Both have working defaults
# (support@airrow.app, "Airrow <noreply@airrow.app>"); set SUPPORT_INBOX on a staging deployment so
# it cannot mail the real inbox — or point it at a personal mailbox until the domain's forwarding
# records are in place (INFRASTRUCTURE_SETUP.md §8). Reply-To carries the founder either way.
# SUPPORT_INBOX=
# MAIL_FROM=

# ── Import digests (spec 68) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pepper for hashing the contents of imported files. Never stored in the database: without it a
# leak of import_files could brute-force a short file (an .env line) back out of its digest.
# Format "version:secret", comma-separated. New imports use the highest version; keep retired
# keys here so older imports still diff instead of reading as all-conflicts.
#   generate: node -e "console.log('1:'+require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
IMPORT_DIGEST_PEPPERS=1:<random hex>

# ── Stripe billing (makes Pro purchasable, spec 99) ─────────────────────────
# Without these the app runs normally and Settings shows Pro as unavailable — nothing throws.
# Secret key: Stripe dashboard → Developers → API keys. Server-only; never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# Webhook signing secret. Local: `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/stripe/webhook`
# prints it. Deployed: Developers → Webhooks → your endpoint → signing secret. This is the whole
# authorization on a public endpoint — a wrong value means every event is rejected.
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Price *ids* (price_…), not amounts: the figure lives in Stripe so changing it needs no deploy.
# Monthly is required to enable the upgrade path; leave yearly unset to offer monthly only.
# STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=
# STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY=
